        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/lego-drive-delist.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>The <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/esa-e3-california-law-stop-killing-games\">Stop Killing Games</a> initiative, which is fighting against the full termination of games, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/stop-killing-games-european-parliament\">recently made it to the European Parliament</a> and has pushed publishers like Ubisoft to make their games accessible when the servers are shut off - <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/stop-killing-games-celebrates-crew-2-offline-support\">The Crew 2 is the most recent win</a>. Now, 2K games is delisting casual racing game <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/lego-2k-drive\">Lego 2K Drive</a> this week, but it'll remain playable online for another year and work offline once support ends.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/lego-2k-drive-delisting\">Read more</a></p>",
